Bound the session bus read of the writer

A stalled session bus parks a write pass for ever. The pass asks the
portal for the GTK theme name over the bus. A bus that accepts the
call and never answers holds the main thread on a lock of Qt that has
no deadline. No exit code and no file lock can then reach the pass.

The theme read now runs in a sacrificial thread under a deadline. A
read that answers gives the name to the pass. A read that meets the
deadline stops the pass with a code of its own. The pass deletes no
file, because a bus that gives no name is not a foreign theme. At most
one such thread stays blocked, because a later read stops at once and
names the earlier read in its line. A one shot pass that met the
deadline leaves at once, because the teardown of Qt waits for the
thread of the bus.

The watch mode builds its colour watch after a bounded probe finds the
bus and a bounded open gives the connection of the process. The colour
watch and the handler of the lost bus then take that connection, and
neither one waits for a bus with no deadline. A probe that meets the
deadline holds the watch back and tries again, so the first pass and
the file watch start with no bus.

The daemon leaves with the code 0 when the bus dies, so a logout stops
a daemon that no unit holds. The unit restarts the daemon after a
failure alone, so any loss of the bus stops the watch and the unit
starts no new daemon.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
twelfth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15 on
system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

